Well, I've always had this sneaking suspicion that, even if they had to
line up and come down one by one, any monsters not on wheelchairs should
be able to _eventually_ follow you up or down stairs.

It would add a lot of challenge to a ring of adornment +9-and-cursed
if every friendly monster you ever met became more and more pet-like,
and troups of them eventually one by one followed you from level to
level, down either the stairs or dumb-waiter shafts known only to them,
filling every nook and cranny, crowding you, choking you, starving you,
and grabbing all the goodies before you get there.

After a while, that would make cursed positive adornment one of the
more potent curses, next perhaps to levitation.

(By the way, if you wield a cursed tin of spinach, does it stick to
your hand?  I've done dumber things.  My favorite, though, was when
I tried to eat a ring in rogue 7, and a game bug let me do it; from
then on, I had nine rings' powers instead of 8.  Never could get
that bug to reappear, darn it.  ;-)

